  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Swiss - Dialogue Bekaa extension</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">450 beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Highlight the important role conflict dialogue and youth assistance play in reducing social tensions, Establish and advocate for conflict-dialogue mechanisms, Promote new ways to communicate with non-vulnerable groups to deter any surges in anti-refugee sentiments.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The second phase of the Creating Space for Peace project.  The project received a 5-months extension to cover added activities till the end of December 2018.  The extension included the following: (1) The Bekaa Dialogue Group implementing peace-building initiatives, (2) IA conducting a needs assessment to the Bekaa Water Establishment, and (3) Piloting a communications &amp; conflict-sensitive training to the BWE customer-service department.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen and sustain local capacity for conflict mitigation developed through &#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x2DC;Creating Space for Peace&#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x2122; dialogue mechanism. To promote positive relations between Lebanese and Syrian communities, with a focus on youth and women. To promote conflict sensitive water management through community engagement and capacity building of the Bekaa Water Establishment (BWE).</narrative>
  </description>
